'''[[Drake]]s''' are high level [[Slayer]] monsters found in the [[Karuulm Slayer Dungeon]]. They can drop their [[Drake's claw|claws]] and [[Drake's tooth|teeth]], which are used to upgrade the [[boots of stone]] and [[holy sandals]] into [[boots of brimstone]] and [[devout boots]], respectively. These items are five times more common when killed on a Slayer task.

Drakes use both ranged and [[ranged melee]], so melee armour is recommended against their attacks. Additionally, they will launch a fireball at the player's position, which deals 6-8 damage per hit for four hits if dragonfire protection is not used. It functions the same as chromatic dragonfire, although it can also be avoided by stepping away from the target tile. 

Prior to completion of the elite [[Kourend & Kebos diary]], boots of stone, boots of brimstone or [[granite boots]] must be worn within the dungeon to avoid taking constant damage.

Drakes are considered draconic and as such [[dragonbane weapons]] are very effective. They take 50% more damage from water spells.

A superior version of the drake, the [[Guardian Drake|guardian drake]], can occasionally appear if superiors are enabled. Guardian drakes additionally have a special attack that will deal heavy damage and stun the player if they do not move out of melee distance in time, so flinching or using ranged weapons are recommended when killing them.

Most players tend to block drakes despite them being [[Dwarf multicannon|cannonable]]; they have a very high weight, somewhat lackluster drops and high stats for their level, in addition to their two [[flat armour]] value. It is recommended to kill drakes in the task-only area, as while both rooms are still large, the task-only area is smaller for a cannon to make the most out of.

==Requirements==
* Level {{SCP|Slayer|84}} to deal damage or receive a task.
* Access to [[Mount Karuulm]]. 

===Recommendations===
*High [[combat]] stats. Although not required, see the skill levels below for an indication of the advised stats:
** If using [[Melee]]:
*** {{SCP|Attack|80+}} 
*** {{SCP|Strength|80+}}
*** {{SCP|Defence|80+}} 
*** {{SCP|Hitpoints|80+}} 
*** {{SCP|Prayer|70+}} for the [[Piety]] prayer
** If using [[Ranged]]:
*** {{SCP|Ranged|75}} or higher
*** {{SCP|Prayer|62+, 74+}} for either [[Deadeye]] or [[Rigour]]
** If using [[Magic]]:
*** {{SCP|Magic|85+}}
*** {{SCP|Prayer|63+, 77+}} for either [[Mystic Vigour]] or [[Augury]]
* {{SCP|agility|29+, 62+}} for shortcuts at the volcano, if not using [[Rada's blessing]] 3 or higher for transportation

==Transportation==
* Mount Karuulm teleport from [[Rada's blessing 3]] or [[Rada's blessing 4]].
* Using the [[fairy ring]] (code {{fairycode|cir}}) and travelling up the volcano
* Casting [[Battlefront Teleport]] or using its [[Battlefront teleport|magic tablet]] variant, and running north-west
* The [[skills necklace]] and [[Farming cape]] provide teleports to the nearby [[Farming Guild]] just south-west.

==Mechanics==
Drakes' normal ranged attacks can be fully blocked by [[Protect from Missiles|protect from missiles]]. 

Drakes do '''not''' require a fire protection shield or potion to be slain, unlike most other dragons. However, after seven auto-attacks, drakes will launch a volcanic breath towards the player's current position, which deals 6-8 damage for four hits if the player is struck by the projectile. 

* The levels of [[dragonfire|dragonfire protection]] apply to this special attack. 
* Having a form of [[dragonfire]] protection will reduce this to 3-4 damage. 
* Wielding a [[dragonfire shield]], [[dragonfire ward]], or [[anti-dragon shield]] alongside drinking an [[antifire]] will negate the damage. 
* Using a [[Super antifire potion]] or its extended version will negate the damage, allowing you to wear a defender or use a blowpipe.

Alternatively, moving one tile elsewhere when the projectile is launched allows complete avoidance. 

Together, a player can take no damage when using [[Protect from Missiles|protect from missiles]] and [[dragonfire]] protection, if attacking from at least 1 tile away.

